// (Polaris 10) as Linux v6.6 has them. GENERATED by
// tools/gpu_registers_generate.py (do not edit: generate it again; README.md
// beside it says how a register is added) from
// drivers/gpu/drm/amd/include/asic_reg/dce/dce_11_2_d.h and
// dce/dce_11_2_sh_mask.h, whose sha256 are
//   dce_11_2_d.h       7f865912129ac67966827035d5a34b4362f8a3156a56e298cb995386ce77a644
//   dce_11_2_sh_mask.h cd5dde10fcdf14c5355f54dc34c84b7fef30d8864045ae4f5172d7e66beab737
//
// 118 of the header's 10056 registers, the ones SELECTION names, each with
// every field the header gives it (537 fields). A register is its number as
// Linux and the kernel count it, the dword index of its MMIO word (the
// header's mmNAME without "mm"; a register of an index space keeps the
// header's "ix"). NAME__FIELD is a field's mask, NAME__FIELD__SHIFT its
// lowest bit; an enum is a struct of its values.
//
// MMIO_RUNS: every register number of the header from 0xc0 on (below it the
// header numbers the audio controller's own index space), the aliases left
// out, as first and last of runs a gap of more than 16 dwords ends.

